<title>UK: Midland Bank adds 50 mln stg to 10-yr step-up FRN.</title>
<headline>Midland Bank adds 50 mln stg to 10-yr step-up FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following fungible structured floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager HSBC Markets.</p>
<p> BORROWER   MIDLAND BANK</p>
<p> AMT     50 MLN STG   BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY	*JUN.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN    *+20 BP    PAY DATE    29.JUL.97</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   ISS PRICE  99.90     FULL FEES   0.35</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   REOFFER    99.90</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 10-100-1M SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  HONG KONG TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.15	SELL CONC  0.20	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES     *STEPS UP TO 3M LIBOR +70 BP IF AFTER YEAR FIVE IF</p>
<p>		NOT CALLED AT PAR. FUNGIBLE WITH 150 MLN STG FRN</p>
<p>LAUNCHED</p>
<p>		ON 02.JUN.97.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
